b") (hide yes) (uuid "959a8c05-2856-40a8-a1c2-6934ddb081ae") (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify mirror))) (property "Description" "" (at 0 0 180) (layer "B.Fab") (hide yes) (uuid "16de951b-fd6a-49fd-b9e6-f7c675ee92ab") (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify mirror))) (property "LCSC" "" (at 0 0 0) (layer "B.SilkS") (hide yes) (uuid "2643fa13-5331-417d-be7c-8ac5e4d84a24") (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (thickness 0.15)))) (property "Note" "Exact ESP32-S3FN8 QFN56,8MB in-package QuadSPI flash,noPSRAM. KeepGPIO26-32 reserved;GPIO33-37 are usable for this exact QuadSPI/no-octal choice. NoWiFi/Bluetooth RF initialization;LNA_IN is NC. Supply pins stay powered;VDD_SPI pin29 is locally decoupled RTC output and is not directly shorted to AON. Physical51/GPIO45 drives activeHIGH radio RESET_ASSERT through Q746;physical52/GPIO46 drives RXEN through U802. Both are current v2.2 input/output strapping GPIOs with existing external10k R784/R566 pulldowns; separateR815/R816 are retired. LOW through3ms after CHIP_PU rising preserves3.3V VDD_SPI and joint-download boot whenGPIO0LOW. InternalweakPD assists; no guaranteed typical45k resistor assumption. Default/reset RUN on physical47/GPIO41 remainsLOW, keepsradioOFF and OE disabled. GPIO45/46 must remain inputs withoutpull-up through3ms strap hold, then initializedLOW beforeRUN; no eFuse burn. FormerRXENGPIO42/physical48 remains NC. Modem OFF is now GPIO17/physical23 through existing1k R740 and existing10k R741 to Q740 gate; GPIO6/physical11 is NC. GPIO17 is reset input-enabled and has the same documented typicalLOW60us power-up glitch as formerGPIO6; no strap/JTAG/in-package flash conflict. Firmware reserves physical23 as activeHIGH modemOFF, initializesLOW before output enable, and never assigns UART1TX to this pin. MCU reset/blank startup still allows hardware autostart through unchanged defaultLOW R741; recovery drivesOFFHIGH>=5s and confirms modemrail<100mV before release. Independent MODEM_RESET GPIO7/physical12 and independent hardware qualified modemRUN remain unchanged. A new .40/.15 Type7 pole at72.6,9.3 is the only under-U800 OFF hole; receiver68.8,33.1 is ordinary .45/.20, and four routed .40/.15 ordinary transition holes stay outside all primary bodies. Exact factory profile required for each hole, not generic .20drill fabrication. All original power/ground/source roles are separately verified after native refill.  Physical43/GPIO38 remains FAULTinput; physical24/GPIO18 remainsunused due documentedtypical high glitch. PreserveUART0 recovery49/50 and the exact clock/DIO/BUSY pins17/21/22. Radio uses lowest useful GPIO drive, initial1MHz SPI, qualified PG and independent hardware OE/RUN gating. GPIO21/physical27 requests internalUSB only after initializationLOW; physical36 observes externalVBUS. No undocumentedM2UART. Physical14/GPIO9ADC1_CH8 remains analog current observation withoutdigitaldrive orpull. Recovery holds modemOFF>=5s, confirmsrail<100mV before restart; blankMCU autostart remainshardware-backed. New exact .40/.15 Type7 U800 escape holes require both faces planar capped with no proud copper and the literal factory mask/flatness profile; all other transition holes use explicit ordinary tenting and no fill/cap. Low-rate reset/RXEN F/In2/In3/B routes guard actual current571 XTAL three-height return field and all high-current power sheets. A deliberate4.6223mm F0.4 AON source bridge joins Fentry73.5,14.6 through explicitly qualifiedType7pole73.525,14.575 and enlarged ordinary75.49,18.4 source pole to restore physical46/C805 input; exact source/return/125C sensitivity is separately proved. Actual inherited UART/DIO reference fringe deltas remain enumerated without a blanket equality claim. This is layout/source evidence, not powered transient or waveform proof. Modem current monitor: U986 has no separateFLT; Physical40/GPIO35 is explicitly NC after removing the obsolete constantLOW current-status connection. U749 output2 is also explicitly NC while its input6 remains GND. Firmware must not assign GPIO35 to the retired OOB_CURRENT_OK function or interpret that obsolete signal as a current fault. MAIN_OK, MODEM_PG, coarsecurrentADC, actualrailADC and independentSTOP/RESET remain unchanged. GPIO9 ADC1CH8 uses combinedILM guarded1M/100k pluslocal100nC989. Configure calibratedATTEN0, WiFiOFF duringsampling, noGPIOdrive/pulls; >=150ms settle afterisolationenable/railstartup, discardfirstconversion andaverage. Report coarsecalibratedloadbins with±5mV25C primaryADC plusgain/leakage/temperatureuncertainty, neverzero=currentOFF. ActualPG andrailADC plusindependentSTOP/RESETremainrecoveryauthority. I2C1446 source escape: SDA now physical19/GPIO14, former physical41/GPIO36 NC; SCL remains physical42/GPIO37. GPIO14 Table2-1 AtReset field blank, AfterReset IE; no internal-pull claim. Initialize SDA/SCL high latch before output enable, input/output open-drain through GPIO matrix, external2.49k pulls only,100kHz; bounded bus errors/stale state UNKNOWN. Every ADC/control/recovery pin and GPIO21 REQUEST reset correction are retained. One sealed Type7 own-U800 source pole and eleven ordinary tented public150um jobs require explicit manufacturer acceptance; first-board rise-time and stuck-bus/recovery checks required. Local observer1498: physical38/GPIO33 and physical39/GPIO34 are now NC; MAIN_OK/MODEM_PG status is read from local U840 I2C0x41 P0/P1 via retained unidirectional U749 outputs. No recovery/control GPIO reassignment. Bus failure reportsUNKNOWN; actualrail/currentADC and STOP/RESET remain independent." (at 0 0 0) (layer "B.SilkS") (hide yes) (uuid "12b1f01a-e479-499a-a456-28ed5689f14d") (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (thickness 0.15)))) (property "Manufacturer" "Espressif" (at 0 0 0) (layer "B.SilkS") (hide yes) (uuid "41a72b28-011e-4cba-8ba4-6e20fa336a41") (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (thickness 0.15)))) (property "MPN" "ESP32-S3FN8" (at 0 0 0) (layer "B.SilkS") (hide yes) (uuid "adc0ceda-270e-48f1-8d78-f2070f0d053f") (effects (fo